P2 — AI context prompt asks for complaint fields but not existing case matching fields

The prompt says:

include complaint.isComplaint, category, severity, summary...

But it does not ask AI to classify:

new complaint
continuation
follow-up to resolved complaint

So even if existing complaints are later added to context, the AI still will not output the decision type unless the schema changes.

Required prompt addition:

When existing complaint cases are provided, decide whether each complaint is:
- NEW
- CONTINUATION
- FOLLOW_UP_TO_RESOLVED

If it matches an existing case, include matchedIssueId.

P2 — Complaint timeline is still metadata-only

The timeline is stored in JSON metadata:

metadata.timeline
metadata.relatedCustomerMessageIds

but it is weak for real case management.

Problems:

timeline capped at 50 entries
hard to paginate
hard to query
hard to build analytics
hard to audit individual message-to-complaint links

Recommended table:

CustomerIssueTimelineEvent {
  id
  businessId
  issueId
  messageId?
  actorMembershipId?
  type
  summary
  metadata
  createdAt
}

And/or:

CustomerIssueMessage {
  id
  businessId
  issueId
  messageId
  relationType: "CREATED_FROM" | "MATCHED_FOLLOW_UP" | "REOPENED_BY"
  createdAt
}

Not a merge blocker if this is MVP, but it matters for Premium analytics later.